  <!-- 9. RM_ChillStillbloom — solution-phase flower, deep floor. 🔴 defName
       is RM_ChillStillbloom, NOT the bare RM_Stillbloom the doc's own
       collision check claimed was free ("All ten defNames collision-checked
       against src/ and design/... every one FREE") — MEASURED false this
       pass: src/RimMandrake/TerminalBiomes/Defs/ThingDefs_Plants/
       RM_GreySeaUnderstorey.xml already defines defName RM_Stillbloom (a
       different plant, the Grey Sea's own bone-white pool-surface bloom).
       A duplicate defName discards one of the two defs entirely
       (load-order dependent, silent). Renamed the defName only — label
       stays "stillbloom" (flavour text, no collision risk; two biomes are
       allowed to have visually/thematically similar blooms under the same
       common name). Correction also owed to the design doc's own false
       "every one FREE" claim (correctness outranks seat ownership).

       Solution-phase life: dissolved as its default state. RULED (Q6, "warm
       bloom, both edges"): flowers in a heat plume's outer ring while the
       innermost cells boil bare. Implemented via vanilla
       min/maxGrowthTemperature ALONE, no new MapComponent — the same
       physical mechanism RM_MapComponent_ChillBoilShroud grades cells by
       (proximity to a heat source -> local cell temperature), just read
       through the engine's own plant-temperature gate instead of a second
       hand-rolled grid: minGrowthTemperature -70 (needs real warmth above
       the -110 dark, so it will NOT spawn in undisturbed ambient — the
       doc's "stillest hollows... bloom by the dozen" line is read as
       flavour for the outer-ring microclimate, not a literal
       zero-heat-source requirement) and maxGrowthTemperature -20 (the SAME
       ceiling every other Chill plant uses, so it dies back in the
       identical zone ChillBoilShroud already marks "hull-warm"/grade 2).
       The band between is the bloom ring. Constitutively unharvestable,
       per the doc. -->
  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBaseNonEdible">
    <defName>RM_ChillStillbloom</defName>
    <label>stillbloom</label>
    <description>Mostly, a stillbloom is not a thing; it is a region. Its whole chemistry rides dissolved in the fuel, held together by nothing but cold and perfect stillness, and only where the sea is coldest and quietest does it precipitate: over hours, a pale flower crystallizing out of clear liquid, petal by petal, out of nothing at all. Any disturbance and it un-happens, redissolving in seconds. Around a parked ship's heat it flowers in a ring around the warmth — the innermost cells too hot for anything to hold together, the ring just beyond it blooming by the dozen. It cannot be harvested, collected, carried or kept; it can only be found blooming.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/RM_Stillbloom/RM_Stillbloom</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.8</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
